<title>USA: Cyclone menaces shipping in southern Indian Ocean.</title>
<headline>Cyclone menaces shipping in southern Indian Ocean.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, MASS. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Melanie, in the southern Indian Ocean, has become a major threat to shipping, Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Top winds are near 115 mph and it is expected to strengthen during the next 24 hours when top winds may reach 120 mph.</p>
<p>The storm is currently centred near 10.5s/85.0e, moving west at 5 mph. A turn to the southwest is expected during this period. It may weaken somewhat in 48 hours.</p>
</text>
